📹
"Video"/en"视频"/zh-CN"影片"/zh-TW
===
¶Your camera feed, repainted live: as colored letters, as ASCII shading, or as colored squares. Pick a style with the buttons at the bottom.¶

¶Which style button was clicked last. Choice reports the name of the selectable
phrase the viewer picked, and the style keeps whatever it last heard.¶
choice: Choice()
style: 'letters' … ∆ choice … choice

¶Emoji are big, so the emoji style samples a coarser grid. Both grids cover the same
16 by 12 metres, so changing style never resizes the picture or moves the camera.¶
columns: (style = 'emoji') ? 16 32
rows: (style = 'emoji') ? 12 24
cell: (style = 'emoji') ? 1m 0.5m

¶The middle of the grid, which is where the picture is centered.¶
middleColumn: (columns + 1) ÷ 2
middleRow: (rows + 1) ÷ 2

¶One color per cell, straight from the camera.¶
colors: Camera((columns × 1px) (rows × 1px) 33ms)

¶Ten characters from dark to light. The ASCII style picks one by how bright the pixel is.¶
ramp: "@%#*+=-:. " → []

¶Twenty-four 15° bands around the hue circle, so each pixel takes the square nearest its color.¶
squares: "🟥🟥🟥🟧🟧🟨🟨🟨🟩🟩🟩🟩🟩🟦🟦🟦🟦🟦🟦🟪🟪🟪🟪🟥" → []

¶What one pixel looks like in the current style. A pixel with almost no color has no hue
worth showing, so it falls back to a light or a dark square.¶
ƒ glyph(color•Color)
	(style = 'ascii') ?
		"\ramp[((color.lightness × 9).round()) + 1]\"
		((style = 'emoji') ?
			((color.chroma < 8) ?
				((color.lightness < 50%) ? "⬛" "⬜")
				"\squares[(((color.hue ÷ 1°) ÷ 15).roundDown()) + 1]\")
			"a")

¶The picture: one phrase per pixel, laid out from the middle out, so the camera has the
same picture to frame however coarse the grid is, and mirrored left to right so it reads
the way a mirror does.¶
picture: colors.combined(
	[]
	ƒ(phrases•[Phrase] row•[Color] y•#)
		phrases.append(
			row.translate(
				ƒ(color•Color x•#)
					Phrase(
						glyph(color)
						place: Place(
							((middleColumn - x) × cell)
							((middleRow - y) × cell)
						)
						duration: 0s
						size: (style = 'ascii') ? 0.75m ((style = 'emoji') ? 1.15m 1m)
						face: (style = 'ascii') ? "Noto Sans Mono"/en ø
						color: (style = 'letters') ? color ø
					)
			)
		)
)

¶One style button, bright when it's the style showing. The name is what Choice reports
when the button is clicked or chosen with the keyboard.¶
ƒ button(id•'')
	Phrase(
		id
		0.5m
		name: id
		selectable: ⊤
		resting: (style = id) ? Pose() Pose(opacity: 40%)
	)

¶A row keeps the buttons evenly spaced and lined up however long their words are, and
with no place of its own the row sits in the middle, so the offset is all it takes to
drop it to the bottom of the screen. It carries its own backing, since words over a
video are only legible by luck.¶
buttons: Group(
	➡(padding: 0.5m)
	[button('letters') button('ascii') button('emoji')]
	background: Color(100% 0 0°)
	offset: Place(0m -4.5m)
)

¶The buttons ride in the stage's overlay, which is pinned flat to the screen: they stay
the same size and place however the picture is framed, and the picture is framed as if
they weren't there.¶
Stage(
	picture
	description: "camera video drawn with \style\"
	overlay: [buttons]
)
